From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peijin Zhang <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:48:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Resampler: multithreaded ducc0 FFT instead of
 single-threaded FFTW

Resample() ran a full-size 2D r2c + c2r on one thread with FFTW_ESTIMATE
plans (re-planned per Resampler). For WSClean's small-inversion path
(e.g. 2352^2 -> 4916^2 for a 4096 image with padding 1.2) this was ~0.8-1.2 s
of serial work per call on an M2 while all other cores idled. Homebrew's
arm64 FFTW is also built without NEON, and 4916 = 4 * 1229 hits FFTW's slow
prime-size path.

Use ducc0 (already vendored, NEON-vectorised) r2c/c2r_mut with cpu_count
threads in Resample()/SingleFT(), and 1 thread per task in the queued
AddTask() path, which already parallelises over images. Same transform
conventions as the FFTW plans (unnormalised, forward e^-i, last axis halved).

4096^2 LWA test, M2: wall 12.7 s -> 9.25 s, inversion 6.7 -> 4.4 s,
prediction 2.75 -> 1.49 s. Images agree with upstream to ~7e-7 rel. rms
(dirty, psf), i.e. float rounding.

